msgid "Fork [rpardini/docker-registry-proxy](https://github.com/rpardini/docker-registry-proxy) and teach the bundled nginx to handle GCP Artifact Registry redirect URLs (`/artifacts-downloads/namespaces/<ns>/repositories/<repo>/downloads/<token>`). Currently `gcr.io` blob pulls are bypassed via `NO_PROXY=…,gcr.io,storage.googleapis.com,googleusercontent.com` in [compose/registry-cache/proxy.conf](compose/registry-cache/proxy.conf), which is a workaround that disables caching for those registries. Long-term: rebase upstream's `proxy.conf` / `sub_filter` rules to recognise the new redirect shape, ship the fix in our fork, point `compose/registry-cache/Dockerfile` (or its image tag) at the fork, and drop the `NO_PROXY` bypass."
msgstr "Widelec [rpardini / docker- registry- proxy](https://github.com/rpardini/docker-registry-proxy) i uczyć dołączony nginx do obsługi GCP Artifact Registry redirect URL (`/artifacts-downloads/namespaces/<ns>/repositories/<repo>/downloads/<token>`)Obecnie `gcr.io` blob ciągnięcia są pomijane przez `NO_PROXY=…,gcr.io,storage.googleapis.com,googleusercontent.com` w [compose/registry-cache/proxy.conf](compose/registry-cache/proxy.conf), To jest praca, która wyłącza buforowanie tych rejestrów. Długoterminowy: rebase upper 's `proxy.conf` / `sub_filter` zasady rozpoznawania nowego kształtu przekierowania, wysyłki poprawek w naszym widelcu, punkt `compose/registry-cache/Dockerfile` (lub jego znacznik obrazu) na widelec, i upuść `NO_PROXY` bajpas."

